name net-belt-high-1
timeout 320

# WHERE IN THE LAYER CAKE IT HAPPENED. doc/air-defence-network.md section 4, acceptance criterion 10.
#
# One patch of ground, two declared cylinders and two positions on one net: a ZSU-23-4 whose ceiling is
# 1 500 m and an S-75 whose floor is 450 m and whose reach is 30 km. The two zones are the two STOREYS —
# `flak` from 500 to 2 100 m ASL, `sambelt` from 2 100 to 7 600 m — and they are DECLARED GEOMETRY that
# only the judge and the telemetry writer ever see. No module, no pilot and no sensor can read one:
# `core/FBZone.h` is RESTRICTED, which is a NARROWING and not a widening.
#
# THIS FILE flies the HIGH route, at 5 000 m ASL — out of the ZSU's reach entirely and squarely inside
# the S-75's envelope. `net-belt-low.fbm` flies the identical route at 1 200 m, which is the exact
# opposite: under the battalion's 450 m floor and inside the gun's 1 500 m ceiling. The
# trade is the whole tactical argument of Bekaa, of the first night over Baghdad and of Allied Force in
# two numbers: seconds in `flak` against seconds in `sambelt`, and which weapon actually fired.
#
# THE SECTOR is declared and it is a real feature of the defence: the gun answers for the southern
# approach and the battery is all-round, so a bad sector plan would cost the defence its rounds.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   telemetry.csv   zone_flak_in / zone_flak_s and zone_sambelt_in / zone_sambelt_s — the viper's own
#                   dwell, per zone, in seconds
#   events.log      `zone ENTER`/`zone EXIT` with the dwell so far, and `net CUE_OUT_OF_SECTOR` on
#                   whichever member the reported point does not belong to
#
# READING RULE: `objective avoid zone flak exposure 0` is declared and this route KEEPS it — the flak
# storey is never entered — so exit 0 = SUCCESS is the pass, and the price is paid in the other storey.
# The MEASUREMENT is the pair (zone_flak_s, zone_sambelt_s) against the same pair in `net-belt-low.fbm`.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-29 after the spawn-tick frame fix (doc/sensors.md 10, item 24). THE ZONE
# MEASUREMENT IS UNCHANGED — the flak storey is still never entered and the belt dwell is what it was —
# but the V-750 that hits the viper at t = 70.1 now bursts at 7.82 m instead of 11.55 m against its 12 m
# fuze, and 3.7 m of burst distance is the difference between `flight_controls degraded` and
# `flight_controls failed`. The viper flies on damaged and meets the ground at t = 304.9, so the exit is
# 2 (CRASH) where it was 0. EXIT 2 DOES NOT INVALIDATE THIS FILE: the objective it declares was met
# before the aircraft was lost, and the pair of dwell numbers is what it measures.

zone flak    46.62500 6.90000  4000  900 2440
zone sambelt 46.62500 6.90000 30000 2440 8000

net iads
  control ew
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member ew
  member gun sector 180 90 autonomy free       # answers for the southern approach
  member sam autonomy free                     # all-round, and the storey above the gun

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.40000 6.90000 5000 0.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  wp 46.85000 6.90000 5000 450
  objective avoid zone flak exposure 0

unit ew
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 46.62500 7.20000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit gun
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 46.62500 6.90200 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold

unit sam
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 46.62500 6.89800 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 1
